"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1223,"Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Darhami told us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, he is Ibn Hawshab, Sulayman bin Abi told me Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “My friend advised me to do three things that I will not abandon: not to sleep except after praying the Witr prayer, and not to miss the two rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer.” For it is the prayer of those who repent, and fasting for three days of every month.”"
1224,"Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us in Baghdad: Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""No one persists in performing the Duha prayer except one who constantly turns to Allah in repentance (awwab)."" He said: ""And it is the prayer of the awwabin (those who constantly turn to Allah in repentance).""

Abu Bakr said: This elder, Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah, was not corroborated in connecting this report as a continuous chain (muttasil). Al-Darawardi narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, as a disconnected report (mursal), and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, as his own saying (i.e., as a statement of Abu Salamah, not attributed to the Prophet ﷺ)."
